{
  "EvidenceKind": "local/document-derived; not a native RTC capture",
  "References": [
    {
      "URL": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication-metrics-events.html",
      "Contract": "MissedThreshold identifies eligible RTC objects exceeding fifteen minutes; ReplicatedAfterThreshold identifies later replication; NotTracked identifies objects no longer tracked by replication metrics."
    },
    {
      "URL": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/repl-metrics.html",
      "Contract": "Bytes and operations pending and replication latency describe outstanding replication. Metrics are best effort; RTC metric publication begins fifteen minutes after enabling the rule."
    },
    {
      "URL": "https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonS3/latest/userguide/replication-what-is-isnot-replicated.html",
      "Contract": "Deleting a specific source version does not replicate that deletion to the destination."
    }
  ],
  "Limitations": [
    "No native pre-activation CloudWatch query or positive fifteen-minute threshold-event observation is claimed. The native signals capture configured RTC at 09:44:42Z and queried at 10:07:31Z, retaining a 09:45Z gauge and 09:46Z failure count; it proves earlier sample retention, not pre-activation visibility. Phase instants, one-minute retry cadence, immediate local queue delivery, exactly-one local publication and completed-minute alignment are deterministic local checks, not AWS delivery SLAs or exactly-once promises.",
    "Simply delaying RunDueJobs is insufficient: the original attempt remains due first. A temporary failure at the public KMS storage PutKeySet commit boundary preserves real pending work. The wrapper delegates all successful cryptography and reads to real memory/SQLite backends and changes neither jobs nor stored object state.",
    "The live scheduler remains enabled. Manual-clock phases and synchronous drains settle due work without wall sleeps. The original object attempt is due one second after upload; the fifteenth-minute notification is therefore strictly before its next minute-spaced retry.",
    "AWS documents NotTracked broadly; cancellation by an explicit source-version deletion before replication is a document-derived local interpretation, not a positive native NotTracked capture.",
    "Reporting begins fifteen minutes after rule configuration, independently of object age. Notification configuration is allowed two local minutes to propagate before uploads. Pre-activation queries require all four RTC metrics to be absent while sampling and real replication attempts continue.",
    "Pending work, withheld samples/counters and the threshold-reported fence are reconstructed through retainedCloud on both backends; SQLite closes and reopens the actual database. An explicit destination-policy denial produces a real early terminal failure under the same rule. Completed/canceled/failed jobs must not create later events or additional object versions.",
    "Setup replaces an unsampled metrics-only schedule with RTC before object admission. Future sampling takes the new activation deadline; already sampled/counter observations retain their accepted publication deadline. This is a local configuration-transition regression, not a separate native timing capture."
  ],
